Subtask 5.2: Manage Update Maintenance Windows
Create a maintenance window schedule:
# Create maintenance window for weekend updates
hammer maintenance-window create \
  --name "Weekend Maintenance" \
  --start-time "2024-01-20 02:00:00" \
  --end-time "2024-01-20 06:00:00" \
  --recurring weekly

# Assign hosts to maintenance window
hammer maintenance-window add-host \
  --name "Weekend Maintenance" \
  --host client1.example.com
Schedule updates within maintenance windows:
# Schedule job during maintenance window
hammer job-invocation create \
  --job-template "Apply Errata - Katello Script Default" \
  --search-query "name = client1.example.com" \
  --start-at "2024-01-20 02:30:00" \
  --inputs "errata=security"
Troubleshooting Common Issues
Issue 1: Job Fails with Package Conflicts
Symptoms: Update job fails with dependency resolution errors

Solution:

# Check for conflicting packages
hammer host package list --host client1.example.com --search "upgradable=true"

# Resolve conflicts by updating all related packages
hammer job-invocation create \
  --job-template "Package Action - Katello Script Default" \
  --search-query "name = client1.example.com" \
  --inputs "action=update,package=*"
Issue 2: Host Not Receiving Updates
Symptoms: No errata showing for registered host

Solution:

Verify host subscription status:
hammer host subscription list --host client1.example.com
Check content view assignment:
hammer host info --name client1.example.com --fields "Content view,Lifecycle environment"
Refresh host package profile:
hammer host refresh-facts --name client1.example.com
Issue 3: Slow Update Performance
Symptoms: Updates taking excessive time to complete

Solution:

Check Satellite server resources and tune settings
Configure local repository mirrors
Adjust concurrent job limits:
# Modify foreman settings for better performance
hammer settings set --name "foreman_tasks_proxy_batch_size" --value "10"
hammer settings set --name "katello_applicability_batch_size" --value "50"
